# Groundwork settings — copy the lines you need into the real file and edit
# there, not here:
#   native install:  .env in the repo root
#   Docker:          docker/data/config/.env  (sourced on container start;
#                    never bind-mount the FILE itself — docker/README.md says why)
# Every setting has a working default. An empty file is a valid file.

# --- first account -----------------------------------------------------------
# The normal path is the setup wizard: open the web UI on a fresh install and
# it walks you through creating the admin. This pair is the HEADLESS
# alternative only. Bootstrap runs once, and only while ZERO accounts exist —
# after that it is ignored, so it can never reset anyone's password. Weak
# passwords are refused ("changeme", anything under 8 characters).
#GW_ADMIN_USER=admin
#GW_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# --- machine role ------------------------------------------------------------
# hq      curates, dispatches, holds the datasets. The default — a
#         single-machine install is an HQ that trains locally.
# worker  trains for an HQ; holds a read-only mirror of the data and refuses
#         every dataset write, so nothing curated there can be lost to a sync.
GW_ROLE=hq

# --- web ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#GW_HOST=0.0.0.0
#GW_PORT=8000

# Auth is ON by default (1). Setting 0 removes the gate entirely — a
# development convenience, never for a machine anyone else can reach.
#GW_AUTH=1

# How OTHER machines reach this one (pairing, sync, dispatch). Left unset, an
# interface scan picks a non-loopback address; set it when the box has several
# (LAN + VPN, say) and the guess would pick the wrong one.
#GW_SELF_URL=http://192.168.1.50:8000

# Shown in the UI header — useful once you run more than one instance.
#GW_INSTANCE_NAME=

# --- bot tokens --------------------------------------------------------------
# One slot per project, named GW_<PROJECT>_COUNTER_TOKEN. The cockpit writes
# these (Bots tab) after verifying the token with Telegram — don't add them by
# hand, and nothing ever reads a token back out to the UI.

# --- optional models ---------------------------------------------------------
# Where the auto-labeler's weights live, if you keep them somewhere other than
# the spot the wizard's download step uses.
#LA_MODEL_PATH=
